DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 14

Ansible (Basics + Advanced) | 0–2 Years Experience

Ansible is one of the most popular configuration management and automation tools.
Interviewers use Ansible questions to check whether you understand automation at scale.

 Focus: Ansible Interview Questions (Basics + Advanced)

• What is Ansible and why is it used?
• Ansible vs Chef vs Puppet (high-level)
• What is configuration management?
• Ansible architecture (control node, managed node)
• Agentless architecture – why is it important?
• What is an inventory file?
• Static vs dynamic inventory
• What is a playbook?
• Structure of a playbook
• What is a task in Ansible?
• What is a module?
• Commonly used Ansible modules
• What is YAML and why is it used in Ansible?
• What is idempotency?
• Why idempotency is important?
• What are roles in Ansible?
• Why are roles used?
• Directory structure of Ansible roles
• What are handlers?
• When do handlers run?
• What is Ansible Galaxy?
• What are templates in Ansible?
• Jinja2 templating basics
• What are variables in Ansible?
• Variable precedence
• What are facts in Ansible?
• Custom facts
• What is ansible-vault?
• How do you secure secrets in Ansible?
• What is dynamic inventory?
• How does Ansible work with cloud (AWS/GCP/Azure)?
• How do you run Ansible in CI/CD pipeline?
• How do you troubleshoot Ansible playbook failures?
• Common Ansible mistakes beginners make
• Real-world Ansible automation use case

Interview Tip:
If you explain:
👉 “Provision infra → Configure using Ansible → Deploy application”
you already sound like a real DevOps automation engineer, even with 0–2 years of experience.
